Part A – Open-Meteo (No Auth)

Description:

Fetches hourly temperature and humidity for a given location.

Saves the data as openmeteo_weather.csv.

Finds maximum and minimum temperatures for the next 3 days and the time they occur.

Demonstrates error handling when a parameter is misspelled.
Outputs:

CSV: openmeteo_weather.csv

Terminal prints: max/min temperatures and error handling demo

Error Handling Example:

Misspelled parameter temprature_2m

Status Code: 400

Message: "Invalid variable: temprature_2m"

Part B – OpenWeatherMap (API Key / OAuth)

Description:

Fetches current weather for multiple cities.

Stores API key securely in .env using python-dotenv.

Saves the results as openweather_cities.json.

Tests invalid API key.

Compares metric vs imperial units.

Outputs:

JSON: openweather_cities.json

Terminal prints: weather data, invalid API key test, hottest/coldest city

Part D – National Weather Service (NWS)

Description:

Fetches forecast data from the NWS API for a given location.

Requires a custom User-Agent header in all requests.

Saves the forecast as nws_forecast.json.

Demonstrates what happens if the User-Agent header is missing.

Outputs:

JSON: nws_forecast.json

Terminal prints: forecast URL, missing User-Agent test (status code + snippet)
